{"author":{"id":"1e0a6ff3e01313072cf7b3803c158c22d01a37717237fe198e814e781752b172"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790303434,"nonce":"ksZsjMqnzWdJ7LvMpMrhctJ9kF0=","message":"The review tracking commit records up to three SHAs of *loose* blobs,\nwritten with `git hash-object -w` and not reachable from any ref:\n\n- `thread-blob` -- cached mboxrd of the series thread\n  (`_store_thread_blob`, `src/b4/review/tracking.py:2589`)\n- `thread-context-blob` -- plain-text rendering of the thread for the agent\n  (same function, same write)\n- `prior-thread-context-blob` -- the previous revision's context blob,\n  carried over on version upgrade (`src/b4/review_tui/_tracking_app.py:4432`,\n  `:4616`)\n\nMoving the review branches to another machine (push/fetch) carries the\ntracking commit and therefore the SHAs, but not the unreachable blobs.\n`git gc` can drop them the same way. b4 itself tolerates this (it falls\nback to lore, logged at debug level only), but nothing reliably puts the\nblobs back, so agents following `misc/agent-reviewer.md` hit dangling SHAs.\nThe \"stored git blob is missing\" text is the agent's wording, not b4's.\n\n**1. `u` only regenerates on a count change.**\n`u` -\u003e `update_series_tracking` (`src/b4/review/_review.py:2834`) -\u003e\n`update_message_count_from_msgs` (`tracking.py:2512`). That function\nreturns early when the fetched message count equals the stored\n`message_count`:\n\n    else:\n        # No change -- just stamp the check time, skip commit\n        ...\n        return False        # never reaches _store_thread_blob\n\nSo if the sqlite DB moved along with the branches, `message_count` is\nalready set, and `u` leaves the blobs missing until a new reply lands on\nthe list. (If the DB did *not* move, `message_count` is NULL, the\nfirst-fetch branch runs and the blobs *are* rewritten -- which is probably\nwhy this looked like it worked.)\n\n**2. `f` (follow-ups) only re-caches when the key is empty.**\n`_fetch_followups_bg` (`src/b4/review_tui/_review_app.py:2186`) calls\n`_store_thread_blob` only `if not blob_sha`. When the key is set but the\nblob is gone, `get_thread_msgs` (`_common.py:172-179`) silently falls back\nto lore and the fresh result is thrown away instead of re-stored.\n\n**3. `ensure_thread_context_blob` checks the key, not the object.**\n`tracking.py:2901` and its caller at `_review.py:3310` bail out when\n`thread-context-blob` is *present*, without checking the blob exists.\nNothing ever regenerates `prior-thread-context-blob`.\n\n**4. Agent prompt has no fallback for `thread-context-blob`.**\n`misc/agent-reviewer.md:124-137` says to `git cat-file` it with no\nalternative; only `prior-thread-context-blob` (`:150-165`) documents a lore\nt.atom fallback via `prior-revision-msgid`.\n\n\n1. `update_message_count_from_msgs`: also call `_store_thread_blob` when\n   `get_thread_mbox(series['thread-blob'])` returns None (or the key is\n   absent), even if the count is unchanged. `u` then becomes the\n   \"regenerate after moving machines\" action broonie asked for.\n2. `_fetch_followups_bg`: re-store whenever the local load failed, not only\n   when `thread-blob` was empty (have `get_thread_msgs` report whether it\n   came from the blob, or check `get_thread_mbox` first).\n3. `ensure_thread_context_blob`: treat a present-but-missing context blob\n   like an absent one and rebuild it from `thread-blob`.\n4. `prior-thread-context-blob`: either rebuild it from the prior revision's\n   `thread_blob` recorded in the `revisions` table, or drop the key when the\n   blob is missing so the agent goes straight to the lore fallback.\n5. `misc/agent-reviewer.md`: document a lore fallback for\n   `thread-context-blob` (the cover msgid is in `series.header-info.msgid`).\n\nTests: \"moved machine\" cases -- tracking commit with SHAs whose objects do\nnot exist + DB with matching `message_count`; assert `u` (and the `f` path)\nrestore both blobs and update the tracking commit.","files":null}]}